29:["$","p",null,{"className":"gl-caution","children":"CAD checks pass: one valid body, two aligned helpers, mirrored chamfers, preserved finger geometry and 322 nominal spool-clearance cases. These checks do not establish printed fit or snap force."}]
2a:["$","section",null,{"className":"gl-pane","id":"engineering","aria-labelledby":"engineering-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"gl-pane-title","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"engineering-title","children":"02 / STRESS ANALYSIS"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"REFINED 3D ANALYSIS"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-copy","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"E13 and E12 stress in matching regions."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The E13 model includes the finished chamfers, contour walls, four continuous solid plates and screw tunnels. It uses compression-only wall contact and rigid washer and shank restraints. Sparse infill receives zero structural credit."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The comparison below uses volume-weighted 99th-percentile stress in matching regions at the same nominal 1 mm mesh size. The reference load is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"12 kg equivalent per bracket"}],"; it is an analysis case, not a released load rating."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-table-wrap","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Regional p99 stress change versus E12 · negative means lower"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"col","children":"Region"}],["$","th",null,{"scope":"col","children":"8 walls"}],["$","th",null,{"scope":"col","children":"10 walls"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","Inner seat",{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Inner seat"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−13.28%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−13.22%"}]]}],["$","tr","Knee",{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Knee"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−9.31%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−10.37%"}]]}],["$","tr","Outer arm",{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Outer arm"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−19.41%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−20.24%"}]]}],["$","tr","Lower screw landing",{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Lower screw landing"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−0.17%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"+0.93%"}]]}],["$","tr","Upper screw landing",{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Upper screw landing"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"+1.17%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"−1.12%"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-two-column sr-rule","children":[["$","figure",null,{"className":"sr-figure","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/fem-3d.png","aria-label":"Open full-size figure: Refined eight-wall E13 von Mises stress field with full bracket and cutaway views","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/fem-3d.png","alt":"Refined eight-wall E13 von Mises stress field with full bracket and cutaway views","width":2015,"height":1395,"loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["ACTUAL SOLVED FIELD / 8 WALLS",["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/fem-3d.png","children":"Full size ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-copy","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Mesh refinement and model checks."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Three global mesh levels—2, 1.5 and 1 mm—resolve the complete bracket. The finest models contain ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"757,028"}]," tetrahedra at 8 walls and ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"787,137"}]," at 10 walls."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The last refinement changes front movement by about ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"1.9%"}]," and the near-seat stress statistic by ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"1.1% or less"}],". Independent force, moment and free-residual checks pass."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The E12 eight-wall baseline required a different mesher. Nominal resolution and physical inputs match; individual meshes differ. The full audit records that limit."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/analysis/e13/HOTSPOTS.md","children":"Mesh refinement, regional windows & raw peaks ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"sr-figure","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/fem-sections.png","aria-label":"Open full-size figure: XY and transverse sections through the solved E13 tetrahedra showing walls and internal solid plates","children":"$L30"}],"$L31"]}],"$L32","$L33"]}]
2b:["$","section",null,{"className":"gl-pane","id":"printing","aria-labelledby":"printing-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"gl-pane-title","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"printing-title","children":"03 / PRINTING"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"ORCASLICER PATHS CHECKED"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-two-column","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-copy","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Orientation, solid bands and slicer settings."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Print on the supplied broad side so the main bending load lies in the layer plane. Import the STEP as one object with three aligned parts."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"sr-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Set up the body."}]," Use 0.20 mm layers, a 0.4 mm nozzle, Arachne walls and Everywhere gap fill. Start with 8 walls for the PLA prototype or 10 for PETG."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Keep the four solid bands."}]," Use six top and six bottom layers. Convert both helpers to 100% infill modifiers at their supplied positions; keep body infill at 15%."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Inspect the sliced paths."}]," Check the bands, seat walls, flexible fingers, screw lands and access roofs. Calibrate temperature, flow, cooling and bonding for the actual filament."]}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"sr-figure","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/modifier-stack.png","aria-label":"Open full-size figure: Stack showing the two exterior solid skins and two internal 1.2 mm solid bands across the bracket","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/modifier-stack.png","alt":"Stack showing the two exterior solid skins and two internal 1.2 mm solid bands across the bracket","width":1920,"height":1120,"loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["FOUR CONTINUOUS 1.2 MM PLATES",["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/modifier-stack.png","children":"Full size ↗"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"gl-caution","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"STEP stores alignment, not slicer settings."}]," Convert both helpers to modifiers. They must not print as extra exterior slabs. Check the 207.51 × 219 mm footprint against your printer’s usable bed area."]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"sr-figure","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/toolpath-sections.png","aria-label":"Open full-size figure: Actual OrcaSlicer E13 extrusion paths through the seat and four solid bands for eight and ten walls","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/toolpath-sections.png","alt":"Actual OrcaSlicer E13 extrusion paths through the seat and four solid bands for eight and ten walls","width":1950,"height":1350,"loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["ACTUAL ORCASLICER PATHS / BOTH WALL COUNTS",["$","a",null,{"href":"/spool-wall-rack/assets/toolpath-sections.png","children":"Full size ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-copy","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Both reference slices pass all 120 layers and all 24 intended solid-band layers, with sampled checks of the full planes, seat walls and fingers. Slicing does not qualify physical bonding, bridging or curling."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/designs/closed-wall-e13/README.md","children":"Detailed print handoff & verification records ↗"}]]}]]}]
2c:["$","section",null,{"className":"gl-pane","id":"downloads","aria-labelledby":"downloads-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"gl-pane-title","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"downloads-title","children":"04 / DOWNLOADS"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"E13 DOWNLOADS"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-two-column","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-copy","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Start with the assembled STEP."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The main body and both infill helpers retain their alignment. The STL bundle is a fallback if the importer loses those parts."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sr-actions","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"gl-button sr-primary","href":"/spool-wall-rack/downloads/bracket-with-modifier-helpers.step","download":true,"children":"STEP with aligned helpers ↓"}],["$","a",null,{"className":"gl-button","href":"/spool-wall-rack/downloads/e13-stl-bundle.zip","download":true,"children":"STL bundle ↓"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"sr-caption","children":"STEP: 15.25 MB · millimeters · geometry only. STL bundle: body-only.stl, helper-1.stl and helper-2.stl with setup notes."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"gl-link-list","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/README.md","children":["Complete print & engineering guide",["$","span",null,{"children":"↗"}]]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/fit/README.md","children":["Fit coupons & measurement plan",["$","span",null,{"children":"↗"}]]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/analysis/e13/README.md","children":["Reproduce the analysis",["$","span",null,{"children":"↗"}]]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/thereprocase/spool-wall-rack/blob/5e95cbf5544b205bdf2b73611d24ce3f826e837d/analysis/e13/r